      "severity": "moderate",
      "explanation": "Fluconazole is a known inhibitor of CYP2C9, which is a primary enzyme responsible for the metabolism of the more potent S-enantiomer of warfarin. Concomitant use can increase warfarin exposure and INR, necessitating closer monitoring.",
      "recommendation": "Closely monitor INR if a concomitant drug is a CYP2C9, 1A2, and/or 3A4 inhibitor or inducer. More frequent INR monitoring should be performed when starting or stopping other drugs.",
